Translation patch: combinators taking functions or closures, and iterator adaptors (binlog)

Change: In binlog/events/*, binlog/mod.rs (`ColumnType::get_metadata`), binlog/value.rs and binlog/row.rs: `.map(Self)`, `.map(RawConst::get).transpose()`, `.map(RawConst::new)`, `.map(BinlogValue::Value)`, `.map(datetime_from_packed)`, `.ok_or_else(unexpected_buf_eof)?`, `.map(|x| ..)`, `.and_then(|x| ..)`, `.map_err(BadColumnType::from)`, `?` on `Option` in `get_metadata`, and `.filter(..).count()` (`TableMapEvent::json_column_count`) become explicit `match`es (with `return` where they were followed by `?`) and an index loop.
Why: As in patches 09, 13 and 53: Aeneas fails on functions/constructors used as values, does not model closures passed to these combinators, `?` on `Option`, nor iterator adaptors.
Behaviour: Identical: each `match` is the definition of the combinator; the loop counts the same elements.

